{
  "schema_version": "1.0.0",
  "edition_id": "WEBSTER1833",
  "book_code": "JOB",
  "chapter": 39,
  "verses": [
    {
      "id": "JOB.39.1",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.39.1",
      "verse": 1,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Knowest thou the time when the wild goats of the rock bring forth? ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "or",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " canst thou mark when the hinds do calve?",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.39.2",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.39.2",
      "verse": 2,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Canst thou number the months ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "that",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " they fulfill? or knowest thou the time when they bring forth?",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.39.3",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.39.3",
      "verse": 3,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "They bow themselves, they bring forth their young ones, they cast out their sorrows.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.39.4",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.39.4",
      "verse": 4,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Their young ones are in good liking, they grow up with corn; they go forth, and return not to them.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.39.5",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.39.5",
      "verse": 5,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Who hath sent out the wild ass free? or who hath loosed the bands of the wild ass?",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.39.6",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.39.6",
      "verse": 6,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Whose house I have made the wilderness, and the barren land his dwellings.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.39.7",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.39.7",
      "verse": 7,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "He scorneth the multitude of the city, neither regardeth he the crying of the driver.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.39.8",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.39.8",
      "verse": 8,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "The range of the mountains ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " his pasture, and he searcheth after every green thing.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.39.9",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.39.9",
      "verse": 9,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Will the unicorn be willing to serve thee, or abide by thy crib?",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.39.10",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.39.10",
      "verse": 10,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Canst thou bind the unicorn with his band in the furrow? or will he harrow the valleys after thee?",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.39.11",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.39.11",
      "verse": 11,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Wilt thou trust him, because his strength ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " great? or wilt thou leave thy labor to him?",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.39.12",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.39.12",
      "verse": 12,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Wilt thou believe him, that he will bring home thy seed, and gather ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "it into",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " thy barn?",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.39.13",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.39.13",
      "verse": 13,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Gavest thou",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " the goodly wings to the peacocks? or wings and feathers to the ostrich!",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.39.14",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.39.14",
      "verse": 14,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Which leaveth her eggs in the earth, and warmeth them in the dust,",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.39.15",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.39.15",
      "verse": 15,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And forgetteth that the foot may crush them, or that the wild beast may break them.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.39.16",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.39.16",
      "verse": 16,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "She is hardened against her young ones, as though ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "they were",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " not hers: her labor is in vain without fear;",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.39.17",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.39.17",
      "verse": 17,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Because God hath withheld wisdom from her, neither hath he imparted to her understanding.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.39.18",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.39.18",
      "verse": 18,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "When she lifteth herself on high, she scorneth the horse and his rider.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.39.19",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.39.19",
      "verse": 19,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Hast thou given the horse strength? hast thou clothed his neck with thunder?",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.39.20",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.39.20",
      "verse": 20,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Canst thou make him afraid as a grasshopper? the glory of his nostrils ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " terrible.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.39.21",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.39.21",
      "verse": 21,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "He paweth in the valley, and rejoiceth in ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "his",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " strength: he goeth on to meet the armed men.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.39.22",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.39.22",
      "verse": 22,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "He mocketh at fear, and is not affrighted; neither turneth he back from the sword.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.39.23",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.39.23",
      "verse": 23,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "The quiver rattleth against him, the glittering spear and the shield.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.39.24",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.39.24",
      "verse": 24,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "He swalloweth the ground with fierceness and rage: neither believeth he that ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "it is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " the sound of the trumpet.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.39.25",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.39.25",
      "verse": 25,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "He saith among the trumpets, Ha, ha; and he smelleth the battle afar off, the thunder of the captains, and the shouting.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.39.26",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.39.26",
      "verse": 26,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Doth the hawk fly by thy wisdom, ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "and",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " stretch her wings towards the south?",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.39.27",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.39.27",
      "verse": 27,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Doth the eagle mount up at thy command, and make her nest on high?",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.39.28",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.39.28",
      "verse": 28,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "She dwelleth and abideth on the rock, upon the crag of the rock, and the strong place.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.39.29",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.39.29",
      "verse": 29,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "From thence she seeketh the prey, ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "and",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " her eyes behold afar off.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.39.30",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.39.30",
      "verse": 30,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Her young ones also suck up blood: and where the slain ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "are",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": ", there ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " she.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    }
  ]
}
